[gd_scene load_steps=21 format=3]

; Ocean drift — sparse natural flotsam that turns as the turtle swims through it.
;
; This used to be a man-made litter kit (a 0.5 m plastic bag plane, a tin can, a
; cork, a 0.5 m wood plank and a metal gleam chip) at 40 pieces per pocket. Three
; pockets per level meant ~120 large, hard-edged objects crammed into the swim
; lane, which read as visual garbage and were the worst-looking thing on screen.
;
; It is now soft alpha sprites of kelp / seagrass / shells plus two tiny solids,
; spread over a wider box at roughly a quarter of the count, with an alpha ramp
; so pieces fade in and out instead of popping.

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/effects/ocean_debris.gd" id="deb_script"]
[ext_resource type="Texture2D" path="res://assets/textures/flotsam/kelp_frond.png" id="tex_kelp"]
